A second, smaller ask in the same file, if it is welcome:

`redis` at line 71 is `command: redis-server --save 60 1 --loglevel warning`,
with no way to give it a password from outside. The service correctly binds
`${REDIS_BIND_HOST:-127.0.0.1}` — the comment above it even explains why
exposing it without `--requirepass` would be dangerous — but a deployment that
wants defence in depth on its own compose network has no lever at all. The
same shape would work:

    command: redis-server --save 60 1 --loglevel warning
             ${REDIS_PASSWORD:+--requirepass "$REDIS_PASSWORD"}

or an explicit `REDIS_PASSWORD` variable threaded through, whichever fits the
project's conventions better.
